# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
.git
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml
**/.venv
**/.hypothesis
**/.ruff_cache
voter-app/build
voter-app/dist
voter-app/coverage
voter-app/test-results
voter-app/playwright-report
graphify-out
ci-local
flask_voter_app
**/.env
**/.env.*

# fast_api_voter local-only artifacts (all gitignored, see .gitignore's own
# comments for why each exists). Found for real, not by inspection: `.git` is
# excluded above for a small/reproducible build context, but ruff/most tools
# respect `.gitignore` by asking git directly -- with no `.git` inside the
# image, that lookup silently does nothing, so any of these left over on the
# HOST at build time (e.g. `mutants/` from a local `mutmut run`) gets COPY'd
# into the image and linted/type-checked/tested as if it were real source.
# Reproduced: a stale fast_api_voter/mutants/ on the host made
# ci-local/backend.Dockerfile's gating Ruff step fail on mutmut's own
# deliberately-mutated (non-idiomatic) code, with a clean `ruff check` outside
# Docker on the exact same host state (where `.git` IS present, so
# gitignore-respecting behavior works normally). Excluding these here removes
# the dependency on git context ever being available for it.
fast_api_voter/mutants/
fast_api_voter/.mutmut-cache
fast_api_voter/mutmut-run.log
fast_api_voter/seed.py
fast_api_voter/vulture.txt
fast_api_voter/radon.txt
fast_api_voter/deptry.txt
fast_api_voter/htmlcov-e2e/
# NOT excluding fast_api_voter/fuzz_corpus/*/* here despite .gitignore doing
# so (with a `!.../seed_*` negation to keep the committed seed fixtures):
# tested against this repo's real build context and the whole fuzz_corpus/
# directory silently disappears from the COPY'd fast_api_voter/ tree in this
# environment regardless of whether an exclusion pattern targets it at all
# (confirmed: still missing with the pattern removed entirely) -- while
# copying fuzz_corpus/ in isolation, as the sole COPY source, brings all
# seed files through correctly every time. Not root-caused, and not chased
# further: unlike mutants/, nothing under fuzz_corpus/ is read by any step
# in this Dockerfile's CMD chain (no fuzzing step runs here), so its
# presence or absence has no effect on what this file actually gates.
fast_api_voter/crash-*
fast_api_voter/scripts/llm_test_harness/data/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v5_runs/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6a_runs/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6b_runs/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6b_runs_electoral_only/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6b_runs_recallfloor0/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6b_runs_factor_structure/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_v6b_runs_fs_electoral_only/
fast_api_voter/scripts/sortition_calibration_runs/
fast_api_voter/scripts/acceptance_cascade_runs/
